Things to not do:
1. DON'T PUT COMMENTS INSIDE A BLOCK OF IMPORTS, IT'LL PREVENT THE CODE FROM BUILDING WITH SPOTLESS JAVA
2. When you are setting speed to a condition, it needs to be in the periodic void or the code will get into a crash loop
3. Make sure that your public voids don't have common names, otherwise it's hard to know which one to use
4. If you're making a public static final variable, put it near the top of the subsystem/file so it is easy to find

Things to Know:
1. Comments will help others understand the code better
2. If your code isn't working and your base code was a template of some sort, use that template and go through all the files to understand what the problem may be
3. If WPILib suddenly says that all files are not within the project folder, Uninstall and Reinstall
4.

Things To Improve:
1. Better Commuinication from Mentors to Lead Coder
2. More Comments to make it easier to understand
3. Less Asking AI For Help, More Using Chef Delphi